{
 "source": {
  "what": "Digests computed on 25 Nov 2026 by implementations that share nothing with this package, for the 29 vectors of typed-data-vectors.json and for rows of the phone-key reading (EIP712Document.Reading.signTypedDataV4).",
  "implementations": [
   "@metamask/eth-sig-util 4.0.1: TypedDataUtils.eip712Hash(JSON.parse(text), \"V4\"), the copy installed under ~/Developer/uniswap-widgets/node_modules",
   "ethers 6.17.0: TypedDataEncoder.hash(domain, the types the primary type reaches, message), the copy installed under ~/Developer/THAT/that-website/node_modules/.pnpm",
   "node v26.9.0; nothing was downloaded or installed"
  ],
  "ethSigUtil9Emulated": "eth-sig-util at the commit of eth-sig-util-v4-vectors.json, emulated by that file's checker (it reproduces all 248 recorded values)",
  "rows": "A row the phone-key reading reads has \"reference\": eth-sig-util 4.0.1's digest of its \"twin\" (the same value written as every reader takes it) where it has one, else of the row itself; the eth-sig-util 9 emulation gives the same digest for the row. eth-sig-util 4.0.1 predates version 9's number handling: it refuses 10^18 as a JSON number and reads \"\\t0x10\\n\" as decimal text, where 9 and the old web3swift read both as their values. A refused row records why."
 },
